    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0522" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d196-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-04">4 August 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Former Naval Person to President. Personal and most secret. Nr. 404.</p>
                <p>Reference your telegram nr. 340.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d196-f2"/> On suggestion of
                    Mr. Mackenzie King words “later on” will be substituted for “thereafter” in last
                    sentence of proposed announcement and latter will not be issued until after
                    arrival at <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abraham</hi>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d196-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d196-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission to Washington not indicated. Forwarded by the White House
                    Map Room to Roosevelt, who was then at Birch Island, as telegram No. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">White</hi> 42.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d196-f2" n="2" xml:id="d196-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
